    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8972",
      "problem": "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $5 \\: \\textrm{m},$ $\\sqrt3 \\: \\textrm{m},$ and $\\sqrt6 \\: \\textrm{m},$ respectively?",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV = lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=5 \\, \\textrm{m}, \\qquad w=\\sqrt3 \\, \\textrm{m}, \\qquad h=\\sqrt6 \\, \\textrm{m}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV = 5 \\cdot \\sqrt3 \\cdot \\sqrt6 = 5\\sqrt{18} = 15\\sqrt2 \\: \\textrm{m}^3.\n$$",
